  "text": "Board of Elections | Nash County, NC - Official Website\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account\n- Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nHome\nTranslate\nSearch\nGovernment\nServices\nLiving & Visiting\nHow Do I\u2026\nAbout Us\nFAQs\nPoll Workers\nPhoto ID Information\nVoter Registration\nOnline Voter Registration/Update\nVoter Information Lookup\nVoter Registration / History Data\nAbsentee Voting\nPolling Places\nMunicipal Elections\nMultipartisan Assistance Team (MAT)\nCampaign Finance Information\nCampaign Finance Records\nElection Results\nElected Officials\nMeetings & Minutes\nForms\nElectoral Maps\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments\nBoard of Elections\nBoard of Elections\nNews Flash\nSharpsburg Polling Place Change\nRead on...\n/CivicAlerts.aspx\n2026 General Election Information\nList of Candidates (final)\nRequest an Absentee by Mail Ballot\nEarly Voting Flyer (Locations and Dates)\nLookup and View Your Sample Ballot\nBallot Constitutional Amendments\nUOCAVA Notice\nElection and Meeting Schedule Resolution\nResponsibilities\nThe Nash County Board of Elections is responsible for conducting all elections held in Nash County. We neither favor nor endorse any specific party, candidate, or office.\nGoals\nOur goal is to provide a lawful, fair, and efficient election process to all Nash County citizens. We strive toward providing an election process that meets every measure of the law as well as the demands of the 21st century. We are committed to providing the best possible service and conducting efficient, fair, honest, and impartial elections for all levels of government.\nFunctions\nOur principal functions include:\nEstablishing election precincts and voting sites\nAppointing and training precinct officials\nPreparing and distributing ballots and voting equipment\nCanvassing and certifying the ballots cast in elections\nInvestigating any voting irregularities\nMaintain voter registration and participation records\nProvide public information on voters and elections\nReview and audit local campaign finance records\nContact Us\nJohn Kearney\nDirector of Elections\nLocation\n1006 Eastern Ave.\nRoom 109\nP.O. Box 305\nNashville, NC 27856\nContact Information\nPh: 252-459-1350\nFx: 252-459-1371\nelections@nashcountync.gov\nHours\nMonday - Friday\n8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m.\nElection Day\n6:30 a.m. - 7:30 p.m.\nOnline Payments\nEmployment\nAgendas & Minutes\nPermit Portal\nGIS\nStaff Directory\nContact Us\nStaff Directory\nEmail Us\nNash County\n120 West Washington Street\nSuite 3072\nNashville, NC 27856\nPopular Links\nNash County Code of Ordinances\nOrganizational Chart\nE-Verify\nEmployment Security Commission\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nUsing This Site\nEmployee Access\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by\nCivicPlus\u00ae\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
